#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "b25256b2-09fe-5faa-b27a-bfea7654e8ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-3019" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "5c4164d7-605a-597c-9bab-f6599becc527" :question/math-academy-id "e-3020" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "1d356bbb-b4ad-5730-9bd1-7f3cd151f96f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3021" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119698 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "40927582-03c4-5dcb-b2cc-7c68c73388b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8688" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459249 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e41bba6-7a1e-51af-b804-b4199f30ad81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458786} {:answer/id #uuid "b6af2053-91f7-5fc0-ae28-3fd48c8ccfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458957} {:answer/id #uuid "d572ae69-499e-5678-b918-b83014a1f184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458999} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c10b3b-7a99-5634-b41c-28b71c6d4af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,0,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459004} {:answer/id #uuid "ff95084a-aa85-5f90-a078-a4d05c8efe2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,\\,2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e41bba6-7a1e-51af-b804-b4199f30ad81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458786} :answer-field/id #uuid "000a1a27-f460-5054-86af-d91e26cdbeb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7358da91-8014-5776-8731-ceb0c31740d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129138" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}[\\frac{1}{3}f(t)+2g(t)]\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,6,\\,3⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}[\\frac{1}{3}f(t)+2g(t)]\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}[\\frac{1}{3}f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-3,\\,6,\\,3⟩+2⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩+⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd28227-284a-5a33-8f08-23296c53f5df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-3,\\,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458781} {:answer/id #uuid "69245a2b-24ad-57f6-b7b2-9025bc32aa3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458812} {:answer/id #uuid "89b404f6-abb3-55f4-987d-b91201cfbab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458870} {:answer/id #uuid "90811072-dc3c-55b9-bba4-9fd3bbbf2d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{3}{2},\\,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458881} {:answer/id #uuid "c27ac7a2-3ca9-59a9-a856-170e1f39ded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-3,\\,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c27ac7a2-3ca9-59a9-a856-170e1f39ded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-3,\\,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458978} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd20933-4707-5b47-8e83-30dc4abf3031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "502c15a4-2b20-54ef-9a03-875448a388c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129152" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{3}[4f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{1}{4},\\,-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-2⟩$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}[4f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=4{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[4f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =4{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4⟨-\\frac{1}{4},\\,-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-2⟩-3⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-6,\\,-8⟩-⟨2,\\,-3,\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-3,\\,-14⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099c360b-8d79-50ca-9ab9-2be6125f91dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458634} {:answer/id #uuid "3c597f72-e2b6-5736-9cd8-4ad441b0c2f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458742} {:answer/id #uuid "7c063c86-1d05-5b52-a510-8eb27c05d936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458849} {:answer/id #uuid "828589a5-0183-58fd-a085-df2a11c90c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-1,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458858} {:answer/id #uuid "914182cd-3787-5ba7-8176-7b2df3b7cfec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "914182cd-3787-5ba7-8176-7b2df3b7cfec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458882} :answer-field/id #uuid "b72707b5-f227-559d-89e2-3f13870c731c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b5a16e8-c13d-51bd-9dfe-f5d38efff2fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-129153" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-1⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-1⟩+2⟨5,\\,1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-1⟩+⟨10,\\,2,\\,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,\\,2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459262 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5714a523-c7e0-5289-94e6-462b12492695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5e,\\,{e}^{2},\\,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458776} {:answer/id #uuid "696ef75d-40fc-571f-84fb-862da878c3f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458814} {:answer/id #uuid "9464c6ad-168e-5179-840b-9053f64899f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5e,\\,-5{e}^{2},\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458887} {:answer/id #uuid "9f718c4a-ab8c-5bba-b7ac-1d92388c4df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458909} {:answer/id #uuid "ec643ad8-5f51-5a97-8641-8e98e75405ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9464c6ad-168e-5179-840b-9053f64899f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5e,\\,-5{e}^{2},\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458887} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc3a5736-f96e-55b4-864e-ba44639fb795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94efa4a2-1092-5b11-ab4d-7217c29637ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-129181" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{0}5f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-e,\\,{e}^{2},\\,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-e,\\,{e}^{2},\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}5f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =5{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5\\cdot ⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5e,\\,-5{e}^{2},\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6088ac3-62a3-55f9-9254-bd3af6af7de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388029} {:answer/id #uuid "a26c5fac-577d-55ea-8c59-6e164ae1455b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388030} {:answer/id #uuid "bb49ba41-a2a8-57f8-98f2-980a02993f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388031} {:answer/id #uuid "adc83598-1819-58a2-a620-584ae08d2974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388032} {:answer/id #uuid "c06243b2-433d-5357-a811-c37305881773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-4,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6088ac3-62a3-55f9-9254-bd3af6af7de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388029} :answer-field/id #uuid "8df1086a-a10d-51ec-be27-8b1ada17a1b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b77f59d-ad05-5d0e-a768-18e851546b1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129266" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{0}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,0⟩{|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c5e775-8496-55d3-8f65-268ac9b8e381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458654} {:answer/id #uuid "135bac11-41ed-59ad-b6c8-1343251771ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-15,\\,-8,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458656} {:answer/id #uuid "38cfb223-211f-57cc-a3de-2b0e4a4513d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,\\,-6,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458738} {:answer/id #uuid "8aba1948-9fd4-5c28-a5cd-bd2af2e7e0d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,\\,-5,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458872} {:answer/id #uuid "d93cf475-1ae2-5321-9a8e-2e0fe7d7081a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-11,\\,-8,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d93cf475-1ae2-5321-9a8e-2e0fe7d7081a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-11,\\,-8,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459009} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1308c15-7029-5977-ab04-e6696324bf2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d15da025-4086-5540-bf68-ef7b03d66ed0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129267" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{2}f(t)+⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨10,\\,4,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨10,\\,4,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,-4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{2}f(t)+⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}⟨-10,\\,-4,\\,2⟩+⟨2t,\\,-t,\\,-2t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨-15,\\,-6,\\,3⟩+⟨4,\\,-2,\\,-4⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-11,\\,-8,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb8259f-8c90-5906-950d-4eceda1af95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440580} {:answer/id #uuid "3577fefa-4330-511f-bfb5-e3b0bdd5b2d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440585} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb2546e-95e7-5c4f-8882-4b1f0f221022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,3,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440598} {:answer/id #uuid "a45f0695-37ea-5976-9377-b321aab76838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440601} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf3598f-9c3e-57f6-8286-eee1de57ab13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cb8259f-8c90-5906-950d-4eceda1af95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440580} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ce4d30d-9663-5cde-be1f-6bc470206c3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47592607-bdfd-5d8e-9c5b-5217893655c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129271" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩-⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1770cd34-f70c-5405-bc7b-b9d4f95e4c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,\\,-3,\\,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458664} {:answer/id #uuid "510a2381-6080-5830-8cfb-ceaa0df9ee22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,3,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458770} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c760d4-b497-537f-89c0-c6189aeab7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,-3,\\,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458929} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f911cc-6f46-5833-a95c-f41133ebf040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,3,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459035} {:answer/id #uuid "efba41c7-5000-5054-9377-b76b30b98b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,\\,-3,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "510a2381-6080-5830-8cfb-ceaa0df9ee22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,3,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458770} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b926433-52e8-50f6-bf33-fa54c61d9250" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32ebf6aa-8547-5777-9834-260892a9ca32" :question/math-academy-id "q-129274" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-4,\\,-6,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨9,\\,9,\\,-6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-(-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨9,\\,9,\\,-6⟩+⟨-4,\\,-6,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,3,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2117bd03-1c6f-5cad-b477-24bd9e729cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458694} {:answer/id #uuid "23985b75-b87d-5b4e-ad83-43ea19508d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458698} {:answer/id #uuid "70d83f85-c4ae-51b5-a84d-afc0738bd70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458825} {:answer/id #uuid "a749ad1d-665b-5427-9988-ca625952b300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458928} {:answer/id #uuid "ed479c26-ff80-5972-bd9a-95bf483b94d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a749ad1d-665b-5427-9988-ca625952b300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458928} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc27ed2e-bc72-50af-9261-a3b5d2e0cb7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3643194d-d38f-5e28-b2ac-1e1d3a327966" :question/math-academy-id "q-129290" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i+\\,j+2\\pi \\,k$ \nand \n$c=2\\,i-\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2\\,i-\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i+\\,j+2\\pi \\,k) \\\\  & =\\pi -2\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0735890c-3c78-543f-89dd-6ca5377bb2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,i+17\\,j-12\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440570} {:answer/id #uuid "4be058a2-5710-5ff7-a820-882c2fc11385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+7\\,j-24\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440587} {:answer/id #uuid "4eafeb6b-988b-5aa2-8275-39f0afff0b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\,i+15\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440588} {:answer/id #uuid "9797327b-29d3-5967-8722-3e2bb5aa98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\,i+16\\,j-24\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440597} {:answer/id #uuid "a78142dc-7eec-57bb-a2d3-d7dcffeea81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a78142dc-7eec-57bb-a2d3-d7dcffeea81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440603} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd206ea4-1fa4-5b1a-b95a-d7f9dcd15b33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9dfd8a34-cf86-59cc-aba6-9a0a73cfe2af" :question/math-academy-id "q-129296" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=7\\,i-4\\,j-k$ \nand \n$c=3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (7\\,i-4\\,j-k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5+8)i-(-3-14)j+(-12+35)k \\\\  & =13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13970be9-a298-561f-a13a-5e8d2433bdfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458657} {:answer/id #uuid "70554e11-c9f9-5782-9be5-acbc21451f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458824} {:answer/id #uuid "99c3ca58-d8a3-5f11-ae82-feb036177f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458898} {:answer/id #uuid "a89cfd93-f4e9-50c0-8e1b-60853d6b0f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458930} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb93c26-582d-5e72-8c7f-84a1f899691c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99c3ca58-d8a3-5f11-ae82-feb036177f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458898} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8314db3-fd94-5934-8c57-06ecde0d8fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa2f9f9d-09dc-55fa-a8fa-ab5f37e6b68d" :question/math-academy-id "q-32497" :question/problem "Given that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=2\\pi \\,i+\\pi \\,j+(2-\\pi )\\,k,$ \n$c=i+u\\,j,$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+u\\,j)\\cdot (2\\pi \\,i+\\pi \\,j+(2-\\pi )\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\pi +u\\cdot \\pi +0\\cdot (2-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi (2+u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $\\pi (2+u)=0,$ which means that $u=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f98e94d-1058-57cf-8d27-f13954103a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300023} {:answer/id #uuid "316106c6-12a5-5e17-af69-75de97025a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300204} {:answer/id #uuid "b73bae5f-1557-57a4-b715-8b64982c76c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300877} {:answer/id #uuid "eef1692d-2f31-59e3-870d-7b705a603ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301146} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc4d73d-2ea8-5c78-a393-c5faf89cb3ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b73bae5f-1557-57a4-b715-8b64982c76c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300877} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa59178e-27aa-5b8c-b124-8431df83afc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abace35f-02da-57bf-9b60-2e1f0caa0d18" :question/math-academy-id "q-32511" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k$ \nand \n$c={e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}\\cdot ({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})+{e}^{-2}\\cdot {e}^{2}-{e}^{2}\\cdot (2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & =e-1+1-2e+3 \\\\  & =3-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e12455-ce2d-515b-a4e0-f7b221799cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458620} {:answer/id #uuid "1146d883-a7d0-500e-85d1-a9739b8a93e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458652} {:answer/id #uuid "1a5cfa15-9edb-5bf2-8ed6-6b4167cccdde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458672} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae3ed05-ae40-50dc-b45c-9233daa36cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458673} {:answer/id #uuid "da1a28dc-d313-56b1-867b-e689ed2fee2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1146d883-a7d0-500e-85d1-a9739b8a93e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458652} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6623d6a-9f94-55b1-b5f7-74a8972e6cf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1a63430-5da8-52e4-a931-6317cfed822f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32519" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2,\\,1⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2,\\,1⟩-⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c143a77-e1af-52aa-b7eb-98785edc55ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+2j+24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440571} {:answer/id #uuid "1f61aaf4-763c-5aa0-8b51-415ad9b6527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440581} {:answer/id #uuid "56eb2684-dae3-5d7e-affd-236ebbf2899e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-2j+8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440589} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc32dcc-74ea-50ee-823d-5aefc081089d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+2j-8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440608} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6245d5-3350-59d5-9f2f-1fe8e4fa79d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j+8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f61aaf4-763c-5aa0-8b51-415ad9b6527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440581} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac63dd9f-32cd-5ec8-8fb2-52c021ed5db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e79507a4-566e-5fff-acc4-da31b5f94ddb" :question/math-academy-id "q-32521" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=-i+j.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-i+j)\\times (16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 16 & 8\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(-2-0)j+(-8-16)k \\\\  & =2i+2j-24k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bf7675-80a2-559b-8162-709a1a0d7f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358358} {:answer/id #uuid "52b55dd5-256e-5209-86de-a9c9700d2990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358461} {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} {:answer/id #uuid "e6dcc4aa-84e5-52fb-b4ea-896d476393a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359794} {:answer/id #uuid "ec412725-0d94-59a0-8fbf-bf17919c936a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e28b5a-b897-5ddd-a2bd-d85b9a72bf4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29982efe-8588-56f9-8a2e-657a512dab79" :question/math-academy-id "q-96943" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32fd1c99-c75a-5e72-bdbc-62e3df1f62af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,5,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458725} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab1590d-78ce-55f3-b79e-b8a03c6af2c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,4,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458740} {:answer/id #uuid "41c7b8fc-82a3-509f-bd64-4222260a2212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,3,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458749} {:answer/id #uuid "5585ea1a-956a-530b-bd90-d0d4394646d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458775} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5d7403-6a5c-5a33-afde-3d0beaeb0501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,3,\\,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5585ea1a-956a-530b-bd90-d0d4394646d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458775} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d3e9841-7ba0-53f6-959d-76e8dffb6e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b76a888-c386-580d-abe0-7db8002d6871" :question/math-academy-id "q-98163" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,6,\\,-3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨4,\\,2,\\,10⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}⟨3,\\,6,\\,-3⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨4,\\,2,\\,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f5cd10-e0d7-57e3-b37b-c7277d7967b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-2e,\\,-2,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458626} {:answer/id #uuid "64d609a5-b42c-5819-9f23-9a68661c02f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-e,\\,-2,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458802} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3a2734-32e4-58a6-a431-c5f9c9066c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2e-2,\\,2,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458908} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ce769e-fca1-572e-bc08-de9b48d68f68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-2e,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458984} {:answer/id #uuid "fa1541f3-35cb-5c6a-9b25-9a85e9ec70da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4-2e,\\,-4,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04f5cd10-e0d7-57e3-b37b-c7277d7967b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-2e,\\,-2,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458626} :answer-field/id #uuid "e99b453b-e56a-5891-a94b-5ab07ced0185" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c945750-33b2-55ee-8335-b093fb35e399" :question/math-academy-id "q-98175" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{0}2f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨e-1,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨e-1,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-e,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot ⟨1-e,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-2e,\\,-2,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f78597b-fe94-5d3b-a150-9662a2903e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395460} {:answer/id #uuid "54233a06-2e66-5ab0-bfb0-15ca60c09e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,4,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395461} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8ee068-02df-52c1-8b28-1bce069cc447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395462} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc8b035-a308-57f9-911c-85c571aca7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395463} {:answer/id #uuid "522f82da-1bbc-554e-89ea-d20bd82ed703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f8ee068-02df-52c1-8b28-1bce069cc447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395462} :answer-field/id #uuid "41b5d00f-231c-5d5e-9824-656cae587369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6362c37-2e32-54b3-8aa0-c3cb9e6d3761" :question/math-academy-id "q-98186" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{3}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{3}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨5,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{3}⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩+{⟨-t,\\,t,\\,-t⟩|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩+⟨-3,\\,3,\\,-3⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e44c92-7452-54f7-8420-600f512551e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,\\,2,\\,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458761} {:answer/id #uuid "578eb711-ef7a-54c1-8019-eb596a2fb432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,4,\\,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458777} {:answer/id #uuid "8237db08-8e1f-5711-9993-6c4d8cc3d90d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,0,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458856} {:answer/id #uuid "c29dcc86-ffa8-5da8-9d41-89ae34e0f54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,0,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458979} {:answer/id #uuid "eb207235-b36d-5126-9eb2-a84c0188faec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,4,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "578eb711-ef7a-54c1-8019-eb596a2fb432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,4,\\,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458777} :answer-field/id #uuid "33fb8190-7136-5506-82eb-66d810eb8bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "626ec44a-73a5-5e9b-9066-3e6a39d1e10e" :question/math-academy-id "q-98214" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{5}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩+⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,4,\\,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50576fef-9cc1-59c8-9804-d67805355efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458769} {:answer/id #uuid "6107b03e-74a3-51b4-bff6-9cd58b85ad45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,3,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458793} {:answer/id #uuid "b232e5cf-f1e0-5d58-9885-fe6d5aa08f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,\\,-14,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458947} {:answer/id #uuid "db7716e1-6741-54b8-ba92-22416d6e61cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,\\,5,\\,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459014} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4a0967-87cb-5b21-a446-a276f9858236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,4,\\,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa4a0967-87cb-5b21-a446-a276f9858236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,4,\\,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459072} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7b61c43-f1a3-59ec-9526-9e6eb502bd0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f6b1824-8799-5b59-8e80-5a3b112af87a" :question/math-academy-id "q-98215" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,-5,\\,-6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,-9,\\,8⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-5,\\,-6⟩-⟨-2,\\,-9,\\,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,4,\\,-14⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
